   "id": "q21",
   "number": "21",
   "type": "mcq_single",
   "stem": "There were 4 times as many books in cupboard A as in cupboard B. There were 436 books in cupboard B. How many books must be moved from cupboard A to cupboard B, so that both cupboards would have the same number of books ?",
   "options": [
    {
     "label": "A",
     "text": "1090"
    },
    {
     "label": "B",
     "text": "654"
    },
    {
     "label": "C",
     "text": "436"
    },
    {
     "label": "D",
     "text": "754"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "B",
   "solution": "![Cupboard B: 436 books Cupboard A: 4 × 436 = 1744 books Total number of books in cupboards A and B → 1744 + 436 = 2180 Finally they should have equal number of books. Number of books in each cupboard → 2180 ÷ 2 = 1090 Number of books that must be moved from cupboard A to cupboard B → 1744 – 1090 = 654](asset:q21-sol)",
   "topics": [
    "Mathematics"
   ],
   "fields": {
    "Exam": "UIMO",
